00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,110
Indeed.

270
00:14:39,193 --> 00:14:40,940
That idiot Peterman had it.

271
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,080
Thank you.

272
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:48,620
Oh, right.

273
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:50,960
Let's go, Rosie Life writers.

274
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:53,100
Yes, handsome Rosie.

275
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:56,075
They sure shot a bunch of weird stuff.

276
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:59,066
Probably trying to find
something that clicks.

277
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,460
Here we are. Let's hurry inside.

278
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,080
Sounds good.

279
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:07,185
We need to get Hachi to a bed.

280
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,720
Hey, Chaka, are you here? Open up.

281
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,600
Oh, it's Ray. Welcome back.

282
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,313
I wasn't expecting you.

283
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:19,795
Or rather, I wasn't expecting
them to find you so fast.

284
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:22,411
Hachi was seriously injured in the escape.

285
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,679
Do you have a bed?

286
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:26,057
That looks terrible. Hold on.

287
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:28,375
I'll throw something together for him.

288
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:32,280
You were on Gold Roger's crew!

289
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,917
I was.

290
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,240
In fact, I served as his vice-captain.

291
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,600
The name is Silvers Rayleigh.

292
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,017
It's nice to meet you.

293
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:41,240
Vice-captain!

294
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:46,031
Why didn't you tell them?

295
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,002
Slip your mind?

296
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:49,997
We only needed him to coat the
boat, so I didn't think about it.

297
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:52,140
Wait, you didn't know who he was?

298
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:55,660
Not his face, but I sure know his name!

299
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:58,200
He's in so many books, he's legendary!

300
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:02,560
It's definitely a name
everyone's heard at least once.

301
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:05,220
Gold Roger.

302
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:09,837
I seem to remember a rookie with that
name long ago, but I'm not sure, really.

303
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:13,037
So how do a big-shot pirate
and an octopus know each other?

304
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,120
Pachi rescued me.

305
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,257
I was stranded at sea and he found me.

306
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:20,197
That was over 20 years ago, but I'll
never forget it for as long as I live.

307
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,857
Pachi was still just a
little kid when it happened.

308
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,777
But he saved Rayleigh's life.

309
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:27,277
We remained good friends
after that incident

310
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,477
until he joined up with the Sun Pirates.

311
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:30,972
You ain't Arlong, right?

312
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,555
It's hard to believe.

313
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:41,254
I mean, Gold Roger was executed
22 years ago, wasn't he?

314
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:45,264
How did his vice-captain avoid
getting his head chopped off, too?

315
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:49,000
The Marines captured the
entire crew, didn't they?

316
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:57,580
Oh, oh, oh, oh, man.

317
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:12,580
The Marines didn't catch Roger.

318
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:18,180
See, the captain turned himself in.

319
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:23,297
The government made it sound
like they'd caught him, though.

320
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:27,240
Likely just to look tough,
rattling their sabers, if you will.

321
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,051
The king of the pirates turned himself in?

322
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,440
Because he saw the inevitable
end to our journey.

323
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:42,940
See, about four years before his
execution, Roger began to feel ill.

324
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:47,000
Turned out, he had
developed a fatal disease.

325
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:51,340
No matter how strong he was, the
illness he had was incurable.

326
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,397
He knew that he would
submit to it eventually.

327
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:58,497
But there was one man with the skill
and know-how to help ease his suffering.

328
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:01,257
A lighthouse keeper and
well-respected doctor.

329
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:05,120
A man residing at the Twin
Caves named Crocus. Huh?

330
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:11,802
We asked for his help and brought him on
as the ship's doctor for our final voyage.

331
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:16,680
Finally, three years later, while
managing to keep the disease at bay,

332
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:19,437
Roger achieved what was
said to be impossible.

333
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,260
He conquered the Grand Line.

334
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,320
Did you say Crocus?

335
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:36,260
At the Twin Capes?

336
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:39,680
Oh, that takes me back. Whoa!

337
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,920
That's crazy!

338
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:44,277
I thought the old man just lived
in the lighthouse for 50 years.

339
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,717
But he sailed with the
King of the Pirates.

340
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:50,918
Come to think of it, he did mention
being a ship's doctor for a while.

341
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:54,277
So he was a pirate on your
crew for those three years?

342
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:56,657
Oh, I have to assume you've met him then.

343
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,217
It's good to know that
he's alive and well.

344
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:02,277
Crocus agreed to join with us
because there was a certain

345
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:05,717
group of pirates he wanted to
search for on the Grand Line.

346
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:06,630
Brooke!

347
00:19:06,713 --> 00:19:08,417
I bet he was talking about your crew!

348
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,559
Guess it's a small world after all!

349
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,300
Crocus, you sweet man!

350
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:13,857
You went to such lengths!

351
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:17,137
Yes, he was only a crew member
with us for those three years.

352
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:20,037
But we definitely considered
him one of our own.

353
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:23,591
It's been such a long time,
it'd be great to see him again.

354
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:28,664
So, what happened after
Roger conquered the sea?

355
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:33,491
That's when it all began.

356
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:37,074
The world started calling
Roger the king of the pirates.

357
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:40,968
Before that, no one had ever
called him the king of anything.

358
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:51,020
Honestly, titles don't hold much
meaning for a man about to die.

359
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:57,160
Still, Roger was overjoyed to hear it.

360
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:07,140
Whatever he did, he loved doing
it in a bold and flashy way.

361
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:12,237
Whether it was in battle or celebration,
he enjoyed living life to the fullest.

362
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:16,417
He seemed to take pleasure in thinking
out plans for the future as well,

363
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,853
even though he wouldn't be a part of it.

364
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:24,520
Eventually, as per Captain's orders, the
Roger Pirates were secretly disbanded.

365
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:29,500
One by one, everyone discreetly left
the crew and went their own way.

366
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:32,920
As comrades,

367
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,477
we risked our lives together,

368
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:39,040
but I know next to nothing about where
they are or what they're doing now.

369
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:47,900
Then about a year after we disbanded Roger
turned himself in and was incarcerated.

370
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:52,897
Shortly after it was announced that he
would be publicly executed in Log Town,

371
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:55,517
the settlement in the East
Blue where he was born

372
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:58,977
I've heard that many of
the young faces that bore

373
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:02,037
witness in the town square
that fateful day went

374
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,002
on to make names for
themselves on the high seas.

375
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:11,120
There was a silence that covered the
entire world the day of his execution.

376
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:15,860
I wasn't there in attendance myself.

377
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:24,960
But I hear that his final words
went a little something like this?

378
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:52,160
While they may execute me, I won't die.

379
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:57,740
The world government and the
Marines must have been shocked.

380
00:21:57,880 --> 00:22:00,280
With one last remark from Roger,

381
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:02,757
the public execution
that was meant to serve

382
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:05,397
as an example into
warning to other pirates,

383
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:10,300
instead became the opening ceremony to
what would become the Great Pirate Era.

384
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:16,600
If anyone wants my treasure,
then it's yours for the taking.

385
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:18,220
Go find it!

386
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:21,860
I left everything I gathered in one place.

387
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:24,920
In seconds,

388
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:27,777
he changed the dim
flame of his life into a

389
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:30,780
raging hellfire that
spread across the world.

390
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:45,980
I never laughed as much,
nor have I cried as much,

391
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,820
nor drank as much as I did that night.

392
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:52,100
The captain was an amazing man.

393
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,720
He sure lived one hell of a life.

394
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:05,957
I'd heard it before but
it's still so amazing

395
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:08,677
when one of Roger's old
friends tells it it's.

396
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:11,877
Like it's a whole new
story wait it sounds like

397
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,797
you're trying to say that
Roger created the great.

398
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:17,737
Pirate era on purpose that
I couldn't tell you no

399
00:23:17,820 --> 00:23:23,117
way to know for sure Roger
is no longer with us.

400
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:28,120
It's only the people who are living now
who can create and shape such an era.

401
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:35,717
I'm certain that there are people who
inherited that spirit of adventure from Roger.

402
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,777
That fateful day in the town square.

403
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:40,637
Your good friend Shanks
is probably one of them.

404
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:43,040
You know Shanks too, old man?

405
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:46,946
Perhaps you've heard of a pirate
named Buggy from the East Blue

406
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:49,890
Buggy?

407
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,037
He and shanks served us well.

408
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:55,002
They were both apprentices
on board roger's ship.

409
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:58,540
You mean Jake was on the
King of the Pirate ship?

410
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:02,720
I take it he never told you then.

411
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:08,040
I ran into him again, right here on
this archipelago about ten years ago.

412
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:12,593
I noticed he lost his trademark straw
hat, as well as losing his left arm.

413
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:17,425
When I asked him what happened,
he spoke about you with a smile.

414
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:21,320
I was shocked, Rayleigh.

415
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:22,377
I couldn't believe it.

416
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:27,520
In the East Blue, there's a kid who
said the same thing Captain Roger said.

417
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:30,580
His spirit lives on in him.

418
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:37,780
A Navy warship's been
spotted from the harbor!

419
00:24:38,020 --> 00:24:39,760
Oh no, the Admiral's here!

420
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:55,480
Uh, this is Kizaru.

421
00:24:56,140 --> 00:24:58,260
Uh, I've arrived on site.

422
00:24:58,800 --> 00:25:01,100
Please respond. Over.
